r"""patch_L443_15_spacecraft_room_20261025.py

The twelve spacecraft join the Solar System room, each path solid where it
has flown and dashed where JPL plans it to go (L-443, build B of slice 2);
and the Daily Run stops when the orrery it pulls is not the one in your
orrery folder (L-461).

Built on gallery b1a4ce6c7fc72b17571a13e18ab11df98b86485b at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/tonyquintanilla.github.io (branch main)
and orrery 0c27f47ad631efbfc611a80404095649025687d6 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/palomas_orrery
It runs AFTER the orrery's patches 12 to 14 have run, with the orrery's
maintenance run, and the orrery has been committed and pushed: the website's objects mirror refuses
a drawer row the orrery's export has no key for.

HOW TO RUN: this file sits in the website folder,
C:\Users\tonyq\OneDrive\Desktop\python_work\tonyquintanilla.github.io\
Open it in VS Code and click Run (the same as
python patch_L443_15_spacecraft_room_20261025.py from that folder). It
asks nothing. Then run the Daily Run from the dashboard, not the
maintenance run alone: its pulls copy each spacecraft's plan into the
config, its build fetches the paths, and only then do the checks have
spacecraft to look at.

What it changes, all or nothing:
  - data/objects_config.json: eleven spacecraft entries beside Voyager 1,
    whose two typed flyby windows go (its plan's events replace them);
    the Solar System room's drawer gets a Spacecraft group right after
    Earth's row, the twelve in launch order, five with a label (OSIRIS-
    APEX, Parker Solar Probe, Solar Orbiter, Psyche spacecraft, Europa
    Clipper).
  - tools/mirror_objects.py and its suite: each spacecraft's path plan is
    copied from the orrery's export (its date, span, step and each
    event's window), without the orrery's bookkeeping.
  - tools/gallery_cache_builder.py and its suite: a spacecraft is fetched
    by its plan -- JPL's whole span, the planned part included, a point
    every 7 days thinned where it runs straight, each event's window at
    its own step thinned at its own scale, and the daily tail -- whole
    again when the orrery makes a new plan, and only the tail otherwise.
  - gallery/assembler (render_spacecraft, cache_reader, assemble,
    presentation, render_orbits' comment): the room draws each path,
    solid to the minute shown and dashed after, its marker worked out
    between the served points, in the orrery's colours.
  - interactive.html: the room fetches each spacecraft's positions file,
    writes its text box (distance, the uncertainty sentence, how far its
    path runs) and source line, and names any row the cache does not
    hold yet instead of stopping; its panel says where the spacecraft
    are.
  - gallery/solar_system_figures.js: a spacecraft's distance line.
  - documentation/smoke_solar_system_figures.js: part 7, the spacecraft.
  - tools/headless (Claude's tools): the driver runner hands the room its
    positions files; the drawer walk walks the spacecraft.
  - daily_run.py: after the pulls, each pulled orrery commit is compared
    with the newest commit in your orrery folder; if they differ, the run
    stops before the cache builder and says what to do (L-461). Its
    --check runs that comparison's fixtures.
  - gallery_maintenance_run.py: the live check fetches the new positions
    files.

Success: one "ok" line per file, then "patch applied". Failure: one
"ERROR:" or "ANCHOR FAIL" line and NOTHING is written. A second run
refuses. Undo is Discard Changes in GitHub Desktop.

Written October 25, 2026 with Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5.
"""
